RALLOC                                                         [3.0]
------

Format:      RALLOC [d: [ON | OFF]]

Purpose:     Displays  or  sets  the reduced  allocation information
        mode of a drive.

Use:         If no parameters are given,  then the drives that  have
        the mode enabled are listed.

             If only a drive is given,  then the state of  the  mode
        for that drive is displayed.

             If ON or OFF is also given, then the mode is enabled or
        disabled for the drive.

             While the mode is enabled for a drive,  the amounts  of
        total and free space reported for it by the older,  MSX-DOS1
        style function calls are limited to 32 megabytes, so that
        the sector counts derived from them fit in 16 bits  and  old
        programs (including Disk BASIC) are not confused by  a  very
        large drive.  Programs using the newer function  calls,  and
        commands such as DIR and FREE, always see the real amounts.

             Additionally,  when the ZALLOC environment item is  set
        to ON,  the free space of the drives with the  mode  enabled
        is reported as zero  instead of  being computed, avoiding  a
        potentially slow scan of the whole allocation  table  ('zero
        allocation information mode').  DIR then omits the free
        space figure and FREE prints a note instead  of  the   space
        information.

Examples:

        RALLOC
        A: B:

             The mode is currently enabled for drives A: and B:.

        RALLOC C: ON

             The mode is enabled for drive C:.
